      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Railroads arrived in the 1850s, boosting lumber, agricultural products, and limestone quarrying that defined Norfolk’s early economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/norfolk_new_york",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Norfolk celebrated its bicentennial in 2023, showcasing historical exhibits curated by town historian Mary Dumas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/norfolk_new_york",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s name reflects its early settlement by the St. Lawrence Iroquois before European contact in the late 16th century.",
